-- title:
--   Function field of the O-model inside ℚ̄(X₀(N₀q))
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ be a nonzero natural number and $q$ a prime with $q \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, and let $\rho \colon \mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q \to A$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the structure map of the base ring $\mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q$. Let $\mathfrak P$ be a `DRModelPackageLevel` datum for $(N_0,q,q\nmid N_0)$: a proper, flat, integral and locally finitely presented model `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` $=$ `IgusaScheme.igusaTo (N₀ * q) q` over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q)$ with normal affine sections, together with a curve model `Meta` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)`, an isomorphism `eeta` of `Meta.C` with the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over the base, Galois equivariance of the induced places, the $q$-expansion pin `Meta_pin` on the $j$-finite Igusa chart, smoothness of relative dimension $1$ and geometric integrality of the generic fibre, and cusp sections. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain together with a ring isomorphism $e_O$ of $O$ with the valuation subring induced by $A$ on the fixed field of the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, such that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $q$, and let $\rho_O \colon \mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q \to O$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with $e_O$ and the resulting embedding $O \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is again the structure map. Assume the pullback $\mathfrak X_O$ of the model along $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_O)$ is an integral scheme and that the preimage under the first projection of the open image of the chart $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(N_0q,q)$ is non-empty. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)` such that: (i) for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_O$ and every $a \in O$, $\varphi$ sends the class in the function field of the germ at $x$ of the global section obtained from $a$ by pulling back along the second projection to the constant determined by the image of $a$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ under $e_O$ and the inclusions; and (ii) for every $a$ in the subalgebra `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` of the full modular function field of level $N_0q$, the image under $\varphi$ of the germ in the function field of the pullback of $a$ along the first projection, viewed in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, is the image under `coeffEmb` of the Laurent expansion of $a$ in `LaurentSeries ℚ`.
--
--   This identifies the function field of the Deligne–Rapoport-style model over the discrete valuation ring $O$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(N_0q))$ in a way pinned both on constants from $O$ and on the $q$-expansions of the functions of the $j$-finite Igusa chart, so that chart-level computations over $O$ can be read off from Laurent expansions. It is used in the analysis of the charts at a specialised place, in particular in the statements about node coordinates and about the widths of the charts.
